WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.060
Every morning at the
Harmandir in Amritsar,

2
00:00:03.110 --> 00:00:05.870
a great book is opened at random.

3
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.710
The hymn on that page is read as
the Guru's command for the day,

4
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.790
and shared worldwide.

5
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.260
Beside the book, a fan is
waved over it, as over a king.

6
00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:19.460
Sikhs treat this book
as their living Guru.

7
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:22.860
What does that mean, and is it worship?

8
00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:26.450
In this mission, you'll see the
part this book plays in worship,

9
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.520
and in naming, marriage and initiation.

10
00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:32.830
Then you'll weigh up the claim
that Sikhs worship the book,

11
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:35.010
with reasons on both sides.

12
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.300
Your mission: explain what it means
for a book to be a living Guru,

13
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:41.250
and weigh up whether it is worship.
